{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he said to Moses, I, your father-in-law Jethro, am coming to you</b> — He sent him the matter in a letter in which was written thus, for the messenger would not say 'I, your father-in-law,' but rather would say <b>here is your father-in-law Jethro coming to you.</b> Nor is it fitting that he should say it to him face to face, for he would say 'Here I am coming to you,' and it is not the way to mention one's own name, 'I am So-and-so,' for upon seeing him he would recognize him. And similarly, 'And Hiram king of Tyre said in a letter that he sent to Solomon' (II Chronicles 2:10)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Ramban's point is that the wording 'I, your father-in-law Jethro' reflects the text of a letter, not direct speech."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:00.408713055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}